{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Not with our fathers did He cut, etc.</b> Rashi explained simply, but it is difficult: if this were the verse's intent, it would not have been necessary to say it, since He already said ״כָּרַת עִמָּנוּ״. And according to what I explained in the verse ״HaShem our Elohim״ etc., which refers back to the covenant — that He would not cause His Shechinah to rest upon the nations (Exodus 34:10) — it will be explained in this manner: <b>Not with our fathers did He cut</b> the covenant at all, for we do not find that He swore to the fathers that He would not cause His Shechinah to rest upon any other nation. And accordingly, the statement ״כָּרַת עִמָּנוּ״ was not sufficient, for it can be interpreted as 'also with them,' and does not exclude the fathers; therefore He went back to say ״לֹא אֶת אֲבֹתֵינוּ״, and the intent of this is that Israel merited things that were not promised to the fathers." "<b>All of us alive.</b> It is difficult: but are all those with whom YHWH cut the covenant not alive, since they died in the wilderness? Moreover, not all of those with whom He was speaking were present then, for many, many were born during the thirty-eight years that they lingered in the wilderness. And one may answer that He spoke of the portion, except that this is forced. Further, what does it come to teach us with the phrase <b>all of us alive</b>? There is no novelty in it." "Or it may be said that the verse intends to say that they all remained alive, even though YHWH spoke with them face to face, etc., from the midst of the fire, and not one of them died — and this is what they said at the end: ״מִי כָל בָּשָׂר אֲשֶׁר שָׁמַע קוֹל אֱלֹהִים חַיִּים מְדַבֵּר מִתּוֹךְ הָאֵשׁ כָּמוֹנוּ וַיֶּחִי״, and accordingly the statement ״כֻּלָּנוּ חַיִּים״ connects with what follows it and not with what precedes it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:26.626575771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}